842
00:37:25,640 --> 00:37:27,890
Yeah, so obviously, it's
better to have higher reward.

843
00:37:27,890 --> 00:37:29,940
This is a core concept of
reinforcement learning.

844
00:37:29,940 --> 00:37:31,350
You want to maximize reward.

845
00:37:31,350 --> 00:37:33,440
But essentially,
from the RLHF setup,

846
00:37:33,440 --> 00:37:36,060
we maximize the reward
subject to a KL constraint,

847
00:37:36,060 --> 00:37:37,710
subject to some KL cost.

848
00:37:37,710 --> 00:37:39,980
And what this graph is
saying, basically, it's

849
00:37:39,980 --> 00:37:42,110
plotting it for a
level of KL using

850
00:37:42,110 --> 00:37:44,850
each of these baselines,
how much reward can I get.

851
00:37:44,850 --> 00:37:46,748
And you want that
to be, basically,

852
00:37:46,748 --> 00:37:48,290
as I said prior,
