967
00:42:36,640 --> 00:42:39,420
very much on Twitter.

968
00:42:39,420 --> 00:42:42,060
And I kind of want to give
you my perspective for this.

969
00:42:42,060 --> 00:42:44,200
And I don't want to
sound egocentric,

970
00:42:44,200 --> 00:42:46,325
but I think pretty much
the entire debate is wrong.

971
00:42:49,236 --> 00:42:51,990
Let's skip that for now.

972
00:42:51,990 --> 00:42:53,890
But basically,
there's two things.

973
00:42:53,890 --> 00:42:57,060
DPO fits this implicit reward
function, which Archit showed.

974
00:42:57,060 --> 00:43:00,480
You can think about this as
fitting a particular reward

975
00:43:00,480 --> 00:43:01,150
model.

976
00:43:01,150 --> 00:43:02,350
And there are two
questions there.

977
00:43:02,350 --> 00:43:04,642
The first question is, is
this implicit reward function

978
00:43:04,642 --> 00:43:08,280
as good as an explicitly
parameterized reward function.

979
00:43:08,280 --> 00:43:10,780
A similar question is, for
this implicit reward model

980
00:43:10,780 --> 00:43:12,930
the DPO fits, you
can analytically

981
00:43:12,930 --> 00:43:15,330
extract the optimal policy.

982
00:43:15,330 --> 00:43:19,470
So basically, what I can do
is I can get the DPO policy,

983
00:43:19,470 --> 00:43:22,570
or I can take the DPO
implicit reward function,

984
00:43:22,570 --> 00:43:25,620
put it into PPO, and run
that optimization loop.

985
00:43:25,620 --> 00:43:28,780
Under perfect optimization,
absolutely perfect optimization,

986
00:43:28,780 --> 00:43:32,610
I'll get back the DPO policy
directly if my PPO is perfect.

987
00:43:32,610 --> 00:43:34,973
But that is rarely the case
with any sort of machine

988
00:43:34,973 --> 00:43:35,890
learning optimization.

989
00:43:35,890 --> 00:43:37,473
So we get something
that's suboptimal.

990
00:43:37,473 --> 00:43:40,050
And this suboptimality
induces some sort

991
00:43:40,050 --> 00:43:44,280
of regularization effect
that makes my model stronger.

992
00:43:44,280 --> 00:43:46,780
So these are the two
big questions, I think,

993
00:43:46,780 --> 00:43:48,750
in this debate.

994
00:43:48,750 --> 00:43:52,092
So they've been kind
of tackled recently.

995
00:43:52,092 --> 00:43:53,550
There's this thing
called came out,

996
00:43:53,550 --> 00:43:55,740
Reward Bench, which
is a large scale

997
00:43:55,740 --> 00:43:58,350
evaluation of reward models.

998
00:43:58,350 --> 00:44:01,033
And it has DPO is both a
generative and a reward

999
00:44:01,033 --> 00:44:02,200
model, discriminative model.

1000
00:44:02,200 --> 00:44:05,580
You can evaluate DPO
models as rewards.

1001
00:44:05,580 --> 00:44:08,880
And basically, on
several scores here, we

1002
00:44:08,880 --> 00:44:12,280
have this chat, safety,
reasoning, type of task.

1003
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:15,800
So this, for example,
shows scoring reward,

1004
00:44:15,800 --> 00:44:19,200
scoring preferences based
on dialogue and chat.

1005
00:44:19,200 --> 00:44:22,220
You can see the top four
models are all DPO models

1006
00:44:22,220 --> 00:44:25,580
and outperform, for example,
proprietary models, much bigger

1007
00:44:25,580 --> 00:44:27,530
and sort of closed source ones.

1008
00:44:27,530 --> 00:44:31,250
And on reasoning, the top model
